# Temporal.PlainDate, in the ISO 8601 calendar (docs/temporal.md). Every
# expected value was generated by temporal-polyfill 1.0.5 (the vendored
# tests/vendor/temporal-polyfill, which diff-node runs as Temporal) and is
# the same in @js-temporal/polyfill 0.5.1. A RangeError or a TypeError there
# is a fault here. A case named "deliberate" faults where JavaScript gives a
# value: a conversion of a string, an array or an object, identity, locale
# data, a calendar other than ISO 8601's, or what staticjs does not build
# yet. temporal_test sweeps the strings, the getters, the limits and the
# overflow options further (diff-node compares its lines too).

# --- The constructor

=== new Temporal.PlainDate
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31)
--- value
Temporal.PlainDate.from("2024-01-31")

=== the writer writes Temporal.PlainDate.from of the ISO string
[new Temporal.PlainDate(0, 1, 1), new Temporal.PlainDate(9999, 12, 31), new Temporal.PlainDate(10000, 1, 1), new Temporal.PlainDate(-1, 12, 31)]
--- value
[Temporal.PlainDate.from("0000-01-01"),Temporal.PlainDate.from("9999-12-31"),Temporal.PlainDate.from("+010000-01-01"),Temporal.PlainDate.from("-000001-12-31")]

=== the calendar iso8601, in any case of its letters
[new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31, "iso8601"), new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31, "ISO8601"), new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31, undefined)]
--- value
[Temporal.PlainDate.from("2024-01-31"),Temporal.PlainDate.from("2024-01-31"),Temporal.PlainDate.from("2024-01-31")]

=== another calendar, deliberate
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31, "gregory")
--- fault only the ISO 8601 calendar

=== a calendar that is not a string
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31, null)
--- fault only the ISO 8601 calendar

=== an ISO string is not a calendar of the constructor
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31, "2024-01-01")
--- fault only the ISO 8601 calendar

=== the fields are cut toward zero
[new Temporal.PlainDate(2024.9, 1.5, 31.9), new Temporal.PlainDate(-0.5, 1, 1), new Temporal.PlainDate(-0, 1, 1)]
--- value
[Temporal.PlainDate.from("2024-01-31"),Temporal.PlainDate.from("0000-01-01"),Temporal.PlainDate.from("0000-01-01")]

=== booleans and null convert
[new Temporal.PlainDate(true, true, true), new Temporal.PlainDate(null, 1, 1)]
--- value
[Temporal.PlainDate.from("0001-01-01"),Temporal.PlainDate.from("0000-01-01")]

=== an argument past the calendar is not read
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31, "iso8601", 5)
--- value
Temporal.PlainDate.from("2024-01-31")

=== the arguments spread
new Temporal.PlainDate(...[2024, 2, 29])
--- value
Temporal.PlainDate.from("2024-02-29")

=== undefined is NaN, a RangeError
new Temporal.PlainDate(undefined, 1, 1)
--- fault NaN, infinite or undefined

=== a missing day
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1)
--- fault NaN, infinite or undefined

=== an infinite year
new Temporal.PlainDate(Infinity, 1, 1)
--- fault NaN, infinite or undefined

=== month 13
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 13, 1)
--- fault month outside 1 to 12

=== month 0
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 0, 1)
--- fault month outside 1 to 12

=== day 0, after cutting
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 0.5)
--- fault day outside its month

=== February 30th
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 2, 30)
--- fault day outside its month

=== February 29th of a year that is not leap
new Temporal.PlainDate(2100, 2, 29)
--- fault day outside its month

=== a string field, deliberate
new Temporal.PlainDate("2024", 1, 31)
--- fault converts only numbers

=== an array field, deliberate
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, [31])
--- fault converts only numbers

=== an object field
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, {})
--- fault converts only numbers

=== a BigInt field
new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31n)
--- fault BigInt would become a number

=== the least date
new Temporal.PlainDate(-271821, 4, 19)
--- value
Temporal.PlainDate.from("-271821-04-19")

=== the day before the least date
new Temporal.PlainDate(-271821, 4, 18)
--- fault outside Temporal's limits

=== the greatest date
new Temporal.PlainDate(275760, 9, 13)
--- value
Temporal.PlainDate.from("+275760-09-13")

=== the day after the greatest date
new Temporal.PlainDate(275760, 9, 14)
--- fault outside Temporal's limits

=== a year far outside the limits
new Temporal.PlainDate(1e10, 1, 1)
--- fault outside Temporal's limits

=== a constructor called without new
Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31)
--- error unsupported used only as Math.name

=== new without parentheses
new Temporal.PlainDate
--- error unsupported with parentheses

=== a Temporal type staticjs does not construct
new Temporal.ZonedDateTime(0n, "UTC")
--- error unsupported Temporal types it has

=== a name Temporal does not have
new Temporal.Calendar("iso8601")
--- error unsupported constructs only Set and Map

=== Temporal bound by the program
(Temporal => new Temporal.PlainDate(2024, 1, 31))({})
--- error unsupported Temporal types it has

